    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0089" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.512/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-07T15:00:00-04:00">September 7, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>75. The Chamber of Deputies in secret session yesterday passed, and the Senate
                    will undoubtedly approve, the 1 percent tax on capital, referred to in my
                    telegram 72, September 1, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1-f1"/> the proceeds to
                    be used for the national defense. Such a levy on foreign capital invested in
                    Bolivia would apparently be in violation of existing treaties, and would
                    directly affect Patiño Mines, Grace &amp; Company, Guggenheims, Bolivian
                    International Mining Corporation, and others.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
